WEBVTT

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.500
Old man, I came back.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.310
Like you did before.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:05.990
Kyouko.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.730
You were thinking about your gramps again, weren't you?

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:11.980
Got a problem with that?

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.480
Hey, Kyouko.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.740
Why do you think the old man returned to Tsugaru?

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.240
It was 'cause of his back pain, right?

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.990
Just like you right now.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.250
That's my guess.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:30.000
But you think that guess is correct.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:37.830
After going to Tokyo, haven't you come to understand your gramps' feelings a little?

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.510
Didn't you say that diving had finally become fun for you?

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.000
Yeah.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.230
But I can't go to the next Olympics because of my back.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.820
Even though I was chosen as a member of the Beijing training camp, I got removed.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.030
Am I gonna follow the same fate as the old man?

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:04.810
What's so funny?

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.500
Your gramps is laughing.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.640
He's saying, "Don't lump me in with you!"

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.150
Well, what do you plan to do from here?

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.810
From here?

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.770
I mean about your future.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.840
My future, huh?

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.180
Good question.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:25.640
After high school, I'll get work fishing, marry you,

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.140
have some kids,

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:29.240
and someday buy my own boat—

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.660
You're a terrible liar, as usual.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.150
I don't wanna see you like that, Shibuki.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.410
Your friends are here.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:47.930
Huh?

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:56.420
Yo.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:58.790
You guys.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.930
You look a bit leaner.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.170
Coach Sun has been wringing us dry.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.920
And so we've been given a three-day vacation.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.440
Jeez. At least warn me if you're coming.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:22.850
Sorry, but Youichi said things like this only work as a surprise.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:26.200
Actually, we thought we'd try to find a cheap inn to stay at,

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.750
but when we asked your mother earlier,
she said there weren't any inns in this area.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.390
Don't worry about it.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.890
You came all the way from Tokyo, after all.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.210
We've got plenty of rooms to spare.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:38.720
Thanks a bunch.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:41.210
Y'all didn't even think it over.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:43.720
Y'all?

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.310
What are you laughing at?

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.780
Even you've got friends, huh?

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.470
What?

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.380
We ain't no friends!

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.060
Say,

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.490
how long have you been diving, Tomo?

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.580
I'd say since I was eight.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.990
Wow!

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.680
How many meters is it?

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.500
Youichi...

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.360
Ten meters.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.250
You don't even talk to your little sisters about that?

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.120
I don't.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:25.760
Misaki, Minami, why're you so dressed up, anyway?

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.700
I thought bedhead and shorts were the norm for y'all.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.220
Shut up!

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:33.770
You'll never be popular if you say things like that to girls.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.240
You heard them.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:38.270
Hey, do the two of you have girlfriends?

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.270
I was just dumped recently.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.510
What?

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:43.780
Why?

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:49.940
Well, I started neglecting her a bit after getting a little too focused on diving, and my little brother stole her away.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.280
For real?!

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.370
Yeah, for real.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.290
Hey, you guys, this one's story is even more interesting.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:00.190
What happened? I wanna hear it.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.410
What's your girlfriend like, Youichi?

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:04.850
I feel like she'd be some super-cute girl.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:08.300
I know. I mean, Youichi looks like he's super popular.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.300
No.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.060
What's so funny?

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.080
Like I said, his is much more interesting.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.310
The thing is,

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:24.070
he's never had a girlfriend in his life.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.260
You're lyin', right?

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.840
There you go again.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:30.130
He's not.

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:32.540
What?! For real?!

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.330
That's hard to believe. You're so handsome.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.830
No, I'm not that...

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.540
Stop laughing. It's not like you've ever had one eith—

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.090
Evening!

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.750
Coming!

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:53.520
I know I wasn't invited, but here I am.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:54.350
Yeah.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:55.700
Yeah?

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.440
Shibuki, you're the worst.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.850
You're supposed to invite your girlfriend over for somethin' like this, you know.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:06.520
Hey, Tomo. Have you seen any celebrities in Tokyo?

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.590
You ever gone to Disneyland?

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:11.360
No, I don't get out there a lot.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:15.080
And it's not like you just run into celebrities everywhere.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.370
"Girlfriend."

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.740
When and where did you meet?! How far have you gone?!

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:27.620
Were you together this whole summer?!

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.550
One question at a time.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.050
Are you gonna marry her?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.840
And your question's too big.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.980
But yeah, probably someday.

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.680
Why is it only me?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:41.060
It's all right. I don't have one right now either.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.060
It's not all right at all.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.070
Anyway, how was Beijing?

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.460
It was overwhelming.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:52.320
It felt just as incredible as you'd expect from China.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.570
You got that right.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.480
The world really is different.

00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:02.160
This training camp really hit that point home.
Or rather, I was put in my place.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.330
You were?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.460
Well, yeah.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:10.000
While we were desperately trying to keep up with the training regimen,

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.840
they were doing it every day with ease.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.240
I see...

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:16.610
At least it wasn't all bad for Youichi.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:22.320
Coach Sun was so impressed that he even asked Youichi something crazy like "Won't you move to China?"

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.480
Seriously?

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.390
But you know, I was really impressed by Tomo's stamina.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:32.490
I'm totally exhausted, barely even able to stand, and he wanted to go out and see pandas.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:46.890
It's quiet, isn't it?

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:49.000
Yeah. I can't hear anything.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.760
I can hear it.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.460
The sound of the waves.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.690
I wanna go to the beach.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:11.900
They're fast.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.860
Sorry, Youichi.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.160
It's my fault for saying that I wanted to go to the beach too. Besides...

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.660
I'm sure the two of you would rather be here alone, right?

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:24.680
Not really.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:26.470
We've been in a rut lately anyway.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:28.950
You heard her.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.930
So this is 20 meters?

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.180
This is where you've been diving from?

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.710
Yeah.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:46.940
Since when?

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.190
Since I was 13.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.690
Thirteen? That's only a year younger than I am right now.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:58.070
It used to be that the firstborn sons of my family were brought here when they turned 15 for a coming-of-age ceremony.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:02.560
But my grandpa broke that custom by diving here at 14.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.080
Then I wanted to surpass the old man, so I dove at 13.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.340
Wanna give it a try?

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:15.590
What?!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.340
Leave 'em alone.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.220
Be careful.

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:33.940
When we first started dating,
Shibuki made a declaration to everyone in the village.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:39.610
He said that anyone who wanted to steal me away should come here,

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.370
and he'd only address them if they dove from here.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.380
Wow, that's amazing.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:45.870
Not at all.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:49.870
I mean, there was never anyone who
said they wanted to steal me anyway.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:57.880
So even now, when I come here,
I have to live with the embarrassment.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:58.990
Why is that?

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:02.130
Because nobody's ever turned up.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.640
Someone who would dive from here.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.730
That's right. No one ever dove.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:08.890
Until today.

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:10.640
Until today?

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:13.400
I've been so excited.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.400
Ever since you guys said you wanted to come here today.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.910
Us? From here?

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:25.900
Well, you're divers, aren't you?

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:26.920
It'll be fine.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.390
It's lower than a bungee-jump platform.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:32.170
You just won't have a lifeline attached.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.260
It pains me to say it, but I'll have to refrain.

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:39.050
If I get injured, the two-week training camp will have been for nothing.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.920
Aw, that's disappointing.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.800
But that's a pretty smart move.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:46.910
With that said...

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.940
Youichi?!

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.110
Is he an idiot?

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:55.610
Nice.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:56.940
What?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.190
Don't do it.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.200
It feels great, Tomo!

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.170
Well, but...

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:11.460
But my goal is to beat Youichi!

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:14.210
Seriously?

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.840
Well? What're you gonna do?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.790
Quit joking around.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:25.470
You really were cool.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.060
Back then.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.490
Boys really are idiots, huh?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.920
Youichi, can you gimme a light?

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.850
Huh? Oh, sure.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.570
Hey, Youichi.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:14.280
What is it?

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:16.430
It's not catching at all.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:17.030
What?

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:20.810
Oh, sorry!

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:23.240
Youichi, you're so cute.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.240
You're laughing too hard, you guys.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:36.500
Doing these sorta things makes it seem
like we're just normal friends, doesn't it?

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.020
It's time for bed.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:13:59.020
I'm turning off the light.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.530
Hey, you got a second?

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:11.030
What is it?

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:14.850
Well, I just wanted to confirm this.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:18.480
You're going to return to Tokyo, right?

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.800
You'll come back to MDC, right?

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:27.250
I can't see it right now.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:28.440
See what?

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:33.520
I was told by Asaki Kayoko that going to the next Olympics would be impossible.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:37.560
On top of that, I won't even be able to learn any new techniques for now.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:45.040
So in that case, what should I be aiming for?

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.070
That's what I can't see.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:48.600
I get it.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:53.080
That day may come for me someday too.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:57.130
Of course, the only one who can make the decision is yourself.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.240
But let me just say this.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:02.080
I want to dive with you again.

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:12.220
Well, whichever you choose, at least give Ooshima a call.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:19.480
Apparently, he cried right in front of my father when it was decided you'd be pulled out.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.220
Really?

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:24.730
You'd finally gotten your chance,
so he wanted to send you to Beijing.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:29.160
But when he thought about your future,
he said he couldn't do it.

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.770
Jeez. That's something I don't want to see.

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.560
That man's tears.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:38.000
And what about that woman?

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:38.920
What?

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.320
I mean Asaki Kayoko.

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:42.850
She flipped out, right?

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.050
After I suddenly went home to Tsugaru.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.150
Nope.

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:51.420
She said, "It's something he needs
to decide himself, since it's his life."

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.030
She said that, huh?

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.010
Either way, I'm sure she forgot already.

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:58.390
Huh?

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:00.840
No, it's nothing.

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:01.870
I'm going to sleep.

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:05.090
This is from Coach Asaki.

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:06.500
What is it?

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.610
Who knows? She said you would know when I gave it to you.

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:29.470
C'mon, get in. You'll miss your bullet train.

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:30.550
Coming!

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:33.900
Youichi, if you get a girlfriend, text me a picture, okay?

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.300
You'd better do it.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:36.330
Sure.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.520
See you, Okitsu. We'll be waiting for you.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.910
Later!

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:51.570
Bye-bye!

00:16:57.610 --> 00:17:02.430
<i>Okitsu Shibuki, our agreement has been voided.</i>

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:06.330
<i>From here on, please decide everything for yourself.</i>

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.940
<i>But before that, there's something I simply must talk to you about.</i>

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:16.090
<i>My grandfather was infatuated with your grandfather's diving.</i>

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:22.040
<i>He said that it was different from Europe's rigid diving,
as well as America's flexible diving,</i>

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.510
<i>and that it had its own strong originality.</i>

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:28.730
Why should I have to dive in some pool?

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.980
Because I want to see what that would look like.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.640
There's no need for that.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.250
I'm fighting with the ocean.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.700
That's brave of you,

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:39.060
but it's not so bad to fight against humans now and then.

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:40.490
Ridiculous.

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:44.000
In other words, you're scared.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:54.210
<i>From there, the two of them aimed for the Olympics and underwent a harsh training regimen.</i>

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:59.640
<i>Then Okitsu Shiraha dove in front of an audience for the first time at a national meet.</i>

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:11.150
<i>It's said that all who were watching were
taken aback and enraptured by his diving.</i>

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:22.970
<i>Everyone was confident that Okitsu Shiraha would take home a medal at the 1964 Tokyo Olympics.</i>

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.070
<i>But my grandfather overlooked something important.</i>

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:35.260
<i>Just like you, Shiraha had been doing strenuous dives into the ocean since he was a child.</i>

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:39.400
<i>By the time he went to Tokyo,
he already had a bomb waiting to go off in his back.</i>

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:46.430
<i>Thus, Shiraha never made it to the Olympics and retired from competitive diving.</i>

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:48.880
<i>However...</i>

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.070
ueno station

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:56.570
I'm sorry.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:57.790
What're you talking about?

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:01.070
Thanks to you, I've been able to see a new world.

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:02.570
Thank you.

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:12.580
<i>Your grandfather didn't just lose and return to Tsugaru.</i>

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:17.700
<i>He came to Tokyo of his own will,
only pulling out after he'd reached his limit.</i>

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:21.090
<i>Then he wanted you, his grandson, to experience it as well.</i>

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:26.630
<i>Okitsu, you still have a future as a diver.</i>

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:29.560
<i>Right now I want you to not rush things and remember something.</i>

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.230
<i>Remember that momentary thrill you were able to experience.</i>

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:39.370
<i>I'm sure you realized it then that there
was a kind of diving only you could do.</i>

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:44.680
<i>Say, do you remember what I said to you once?</i>

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:50.250
<i>That I'd show you what your grandfather left behind.</i>

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:55.170
<i>It's not like your grandfather didn't leave anything.</i>

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.880
<i>He certainly did leave something.</i>

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:10.520
<i>It only lasted for a moment,
a legendary dive that enraptured people around the world.</i>

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:18.780
<i>It was truly a simple dive, but being able to capture hearts with nothing more is not something just anyone can do.</i>

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:24.680
<i>That dive was beautiful like a soaring swan,
and so it was given this name:</i>

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.280
<i>the swan dive.</i>

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.540
The representatives have been chosen?

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.100
Yes.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:41.440
We've decided that you and Teramoto Ken'ichirou will represent us at the Olympics.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.550
Congratulations.

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:45.210
But why so quickly?

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:48.560
Also, you said only me and Teramoto. What about the third?

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:52.100
You and Teramoto will be the only representatives.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.310
It will just be the two of you this time.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:56.810
Do Tomo and the others know about this?

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:01.070
I plan to keep this from them until there's an official announcement.
